The upstream Batfish source tree does not ship a separate NOTICE file.
Source file headers carry "Copyright 2018 The Batfish Open Source Project"
and the project README states that Batfish is released under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. This NOTICE records that attribution.

The published all-in-one jar also carries META-INF/NOTICE for the shaded
Jackson JSON processor (Copyright 2007-, Tatu Saloranta), licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. That notice ships inside the jar, which
this repository downloads at runtime from the official batfish/allinone
image and does not vendor.

Batfish is the analysis engine (`org.batfish.allinone.Main` and the
matching pybatfish client). `tools/fetch_batfish.py` downloads the jar,
question templates, and wheel from one pinned image layer. There is no
copy of the Batfish source in this tree.

Other third-party code
----------------------

There is no vendor directory, no ATTRIBUTION file, and no copied upstream
source tree. Fonts on the page are system fonts. `node_modules` is not
part of this repository. `frontend/package.json` and `pyproject.toml`
name the dependencies. `frontend/package-lock.json` locks the UI packages.

